{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","text":"MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"direction"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLUpDown","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLUpDown","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLUpDownO"},{"text":"? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isUnbroken","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"position"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","text":"MXLPosition","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV"},{"kind":"text","text":" = MXLPosition(), "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"placement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAboveBelow","text":"MXLAboveBelow","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil)"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional-unique-id attribute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID that is unique to the entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that specifies an id reference."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"id"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Distinguishes between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same number)."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"number"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The direction of the arrow on the arpeggio sign, if present."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"direction"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"isUnbroken"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"position"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a notation."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"placement"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"color"}],"kind":"parameters"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"MXLArpeggiate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","text":"MXLNumberLevel"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"direction"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLUpDownO","text":"MXLUpDown"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"isUnbroken"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"position"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","text":"MXLPosition"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"placement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO","text":"MXLAboveBelow"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?)"}],"title":"init(id:number:direction:isUnbroken:position:placement:color:)","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"init","roleHeading":"Initializer","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV2id6number9direction10isUnbroken8position9placement5colorACSSSg_AA14MXLNumberLevelVSgAA9MXLUpDownOSgSbSgAA11MXLPositionVAA13MXLAboveBelowOSgAA8MXLColorVSgtcfc"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/init(id:number:direction:isunbroken:position:placement:color:)"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/init(id:number:direction:isUnbroken:position:placement:color:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLUpDown":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlupdown","title":"MXLUpDown","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLUpDown"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLUpDown"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The up-down type is used for the direction of arrows and other pointed symbols like vertical accents,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indicating which way the tip is pointing."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLUpDown"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel","role":"symbol","title":"MXLNumberLevel","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPosition","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLPosition","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPosition","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changed two ways."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLArpeggiate","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The arpeggiate type indicates that this note is part of an arpeggiated chord. The number attribute can be used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to distinguish between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number). The direction attribute is used if there is an arrow on the arpeggio sign. By default, arpeggios go"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the lowest to highest note. The length of the sign can be determined from the position attributes for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arpeggiate elements used with the top and bottom notes of the arpeggiated chord. If the unbroken attribute is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set to yes, it indicates that the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part. This serves as a hint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to applications and is not required for cross-staff arpeggios."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate/init(id:number:direction:isUnbroken:position:placement:color:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLArpeggiate"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"direction"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLUpDown","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLUpDownO"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"isUnbroken"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"position"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLPosition","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"placement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?)"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/init(id:number:direction:isunbroken:position:placement:color:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/init(id:number:direction:isUnbroken:position:placement:color:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"init(id:number:direction:isUnbroken:position:placement:color:)"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAboveBelow":{"title":"MXLAboveBelow","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlabovebelow","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAboveBelow","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The above-below type is used to indicate whether one element appears above or below another element."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","title":"MXLColor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor"}}}